The specification in spec/ is licensed under the same terms as the code.

This is deliberate. The point of the specification is that somebody else
implements it, and an implementer's first question is not "may I read this" but
"may I build on it without being sued". Apache-2.0 answers that in section 3:
every contributor grants a patent licence covering their contribution, and that
grant terminates only for a party who initiates patent litigation over it.

For a standard whose whole subject is post-quantum cryptography — a field young
enough that nobody has finished mapping the patents — that answer matters more
than it would elsewhere.

